cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper it accompanies."
title: "vipose: visual-inertial pose tracking evaluation"
abstract: >-
  Evaluation of visual-inertial pose-tracking pipelines against a
  motion-capture reference, for freehand 3D-ultrasound probe localization.
  Synchronizes the two clocks, solves the robot-world/hand-eye calibration,
  and reports per-frame translational and rotational residuals with
  block-bootstrap confidence intervals.
type: software
version: 1.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/SolavLab/freehand-us-tracking-eval"
